// overlay.marco — the gamer-HUD's behaviour, written in Marco. The native overlay
// plugin (plugins/overlay) renders the HUD and fulfils the Overlay act; it pushes
// the leader-key command (`m + text) as a Commands feed. Run:
//
//   marco serve --host Overlay=bridge:overlay plugins/overlay/overlay.marco
//
// The HUD: backtick is the leader, `m opens the command line — type a route name,
// Enter runs it. `<key> emits a Hotkeys event you can bind below for your own
// quick macros (no built-in ones).

// The overlay UI act — foreign (exports, no `does` body), fulfilled by the plugin.
the Overlay is an act.
this exports Show.        // show the HUD
this exports Hide.        // hide the HUD
this exports Status.      // set the one-line status (a text)
this exports Log.         // append a line to the HUD log (a text)
this exports Clear.       // clear the HUD log
this exports SetInput.    // set the command-line buffer (a text)
this exports ListRoutes.  // list known routes; result is the names
this exports Run.         // run a route by name (a text)
this exports Active.      // the foreground app; result is the text
this exports Heard.       // show live voice text on the command line (a text)
this exports Hotkey.      // run the route bound to a leader key (a text key)

// Typed leader-key commands the overlay pushes (host -> Marco):
// {event:"Run", data:"<route name>"}.
the Commands is a feed of any.

// Voice transcripts pushed by the voice plugin (mic -> Vosk -> here):
// {event:"Partial", data:"<interim>"} live, {event:"Final", data:"<phrase>"}.
the Voice is a feed of any.

// Leader hotkeys the overlay pushes: `<key> -> {event:"Key", data:"<key>"}.
the Hotkeys is a feed of any.

the Hud is an actor.

// Bring the HUD up and load the route list (wraps the failable Overlay calls so
// the script root stays closed; handled once at the call site below).
this can Boot.
this's Boot does...
    do Overlay's Show.
    do Overlay's Status with "ready".
    do Overlay's ListRoutes.
    this is ok!

// Run a typed command as a route. The host streams the route's output into the
// HUD and sets the running/ran/failed status + duration, so this just forwards it.
this can RunCommand.
this's RunCommand does...
    do Overlay's Run with input.
    this is ok!

// A finished voice phrase: clear the live preview, then run it as a command.
this can RunVoice.
this's RunVoice does...
    do Overlay's Heard with "".
    do Overlay's Run with input.
    this is ok!

// A leader hotkey: run whatever route is bound to it in the current app.
this can RunHotkey.
this's RunHotkey does...
    do Overlay's Hotkey with input.
    this is ok!

when Commands reads Run?
    do Hud's RunCommand with input...
        when ok?
            log input.
        or?
            log that's error.

// Live voice preview (Google-style interim text on the command line). Fire-and-
// forget: a dropped preview frame isn't worth logging — it fires several times a
// second, so a bare `or?` swallows the failure instead of spamming the log.
when Voice reads Partial?
    do Overlay's Heard with input...
        or?

when Voice reads Final?
    do Hud's RunVoice with input...
        when ok?
            log input.
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads Key?
    do Hud's RunHotkey with input...
        when ok?
            log input.
        or?
            log that's error.

the App is a script.
do Hud's Boot...
    when ok?
        log "overlay ready".
    or?
        log that's error.
